WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
My instructions tell me
to scrap off 7 stitches.

2
00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:08.170
Instead of using the carriage to knit
a few rows of scrap,

3
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.380
I'll hand knit them and secure the scrap
stitches with an easy-to-remove trick.

4
00:00:14.410 --> 00:00:19.760
Start by pulling out the
required number of needles.

5
00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:26.500
With the tail of the scrap on the right,

6
00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:29.480
manually knit one row.

7
00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.920
Next, manually knit a second row.

8
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:02.720
And finally, manually knit a third row.

9
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:08.240
Now here's the trick.

10
00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:13.560
We'll leave a loop on the
left side of the work.

11
00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:19.620
I've pulled out a random needle a couple
of inches away from the knitting.

12
00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:24.570
Wrap the working yarn around this needle.
Then break the yarn.

13
00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.900
I didn't have a scissors handy,

14
00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:30.980
so I grabbed a letter opener
with a little blade inside.

15
00:01:31.010 --> 00:01:36.570
Next, I'll take each of the pink
stitches off on my latch tool.

16
00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:43.440
A notice that I'm using my finger
to hold each stitch behind the latch,

17
00:01:50.040 --> 00:01:54.520
putting all the stitches on the tool.

18
00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:06.980
Finally, I'll use the hook of the tool

19
00:02:07.010 --> 00:02:12.240
to grab the cut end of the yarn
and pull it through all the stitches.

20
00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:21.820
Notice I've kept that loop on the left.

21
00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:28.300
A when it's time to remove the scrap,
a use the loop to pull the cut end out.

22
00:02:28.330 --> 00:02:32.520
Releasing the stitches and the
scrap can be quickly removed.

